  "assessment": "Warm multiradical, quadratic-reciprocal and conjugate queries have lower medians; initial queries and opaque controls have higher medians. Retained certificates add first-query live memory even when repeated queries allocate less. Sample ranges often overlap; medians are descriptive and no statistical significance or application speedup is claimed. The unchanged full-board limits test whether recursive reuse helps the motivating workload.",
  "budget_tradeoff": "Each recognizer pass retains its 512-node cap. An unsuccessful cache-assisted projection that reused a certificate can retry the original recognizer once, so the experimental query bound is explicitly two passes. A concrete eight/nine-term cancellation regression proves why omitting the retry would weaken a cold fact.",
  "cache_safety_scope": "The retained type contains only Rational coefficients and radicands; it cannot retain Computable expression nodes. Tests cover opaque rejection, zero-new-work reuse, ownership/reclamation, concurrent approximation publication, and a finite width/depth fact corpus. This is not a universal concurrent-cache or bounded-work proof.",
